gate: CLOSED
v:4 c:$ m:navitrack-config role:dev x:tauri
task: S20 T2 — Legal bundle identifier, then macOS build
sprint: S20
dep: S20-T1-decide-unowned-shell-diff.pd
requires: [MOBILE_TAURI, BUN]
test_mandate: ../intel/TEST-COVERAGE-MANDATE.md
quality_mandate: ../intel/CODE-QUALITY-MANDATE.md
invariants: ../S20-INVARIANTS.md

context: |
  bun run macos:build fails before compile. Tauri rejects
  com.navitrack.dut_configurator because of the underscore.
  Set the identifier to com.navitrack.dutconfigurator in
  src-tauri/tauri.conf.json and src-tauri/tauri.ios.conf.json.
  Do not change productName. Do not edit intel that records the
  legacy Xamarin package id. Do not upload. Do not run live radio.
  Do not run the iOS or Android scripts. Then run bun run macos:build.
  If a new host error appears after the identifier is accepted,
  stop and record it. Do not guess a second fix.
  Package manager: bun.

out:
  - both Tauri identifier fields
  - sprints/S20/RELEASE-COMPILE.md

cmd:
  - bun run test
  - bun run macos:build

done:
  - Both conf identifiers are com.navitrack.dutconfigurator
  - bun run macos:build compiles on this Mac
  - The note records that result
  - No store upload and no live radio
  - `bun run test` passes
